<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Tools"
    categorySlug="tools"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Why Every Digital Nomad Needs a VPN</h2>
  <p>
    Working from a beachside cafe in Bali sounds idyllic until you realize you're sharing that WiFi network with dozens
    of strangers. Public networks at cafes, coworking spaces, airports, and hotels are prime hunting grounds for
    hackers. Your bank logins, client data, and sensitive work files are all at risk.
  </p>
  <p>
    A VPN (Virtual Private Network) encrypts your internet traffic, creating a secure tunnel between your device and the
    internet. Even if someone intercepts your data on that sketchy cafe WiFi, they'll see nothing but encrypted
    gibberish.
  </p>
  <p>
    We tested 12 VPNs over six months across 15 countries to find the best options for digital nomads and remote
    workers. We evaluated speed, security, streaming capabilities, ease of use, and value for money.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Quick answer:</strong> <a href="#nordvpn">NordVPN</a> is our top pick for most digital nomads—it offers the
    best balance of security, speed, and features at a competitive price. <a href="#expressvpn">ExpressVPN</a> is better
    if you prioritize raw speed and reliability. <a href="#surfshark">Surfshark</a> is the best budget option with
    unlimited device connections.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Picks -->
  <h2 id="quick-picks">Our Top 3 VPN Picks</h2>
  <p>Short on time? Here are our top recommendations for digital nomads:</p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={quickPicksColumns}
      rows={quickPicksRows}
      caption="Top 3 VPNs for digital nomads and remote workers"
  />
  <p>
    All three offer 30-day money-back guarantees, so you can test them risk-free. Keep reading for detailed reviews of
    all 6 VPNs we recommend.
  </p>

  <!-- Why Digital Nomads Need a VPN -->
  <h2 id="why-vpn">Why Digital Nomads Need a VPN</h2>
  <p>
    Beyond basic security, VPNs solve several specific problems that digital nomads face daily:
  </p>

  <h3>Public WiFi Security</h3>
  <p>
    Coffee shops, coworking spaces, airports, and hotels all use shared networks. Without a VPN, anyone on the same
    network can potentially intercept your traffic using readily available tools. This includes login credentials,
    emails, and file transfers.
  </p>
  <p>
    A VPN encrypts all traffic leaving your device, making interception useless. Even on the sketchiest WiFi networks,
    your data remains protected.
  </p>

  <h3>Accessing Banking and Financial Services</h3>
  <p>
    Many banks flag or block logins from foreign IP addresses. If you're in Thailand trying to access your US bank
    account, you might trigger fraud alerts or get locked out entirely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Connecting through a VPN server in your home country makes it appear you're logging in from there. No more panicked
    calls to your bank while trying to pay bills abroad.
  </p>

  <h3>Streaming Home Country Content</h3>
  <p>
    Netflix, Hulu, BBC iPlayer, and other streaming services show different content based on your location. That show
    you were halfway through watching? It might not be available in your new country.
  </p>
  <p>
    A VPN lets you connect through servers in your home country, unlocking your full content library. All VPNs we
    recommend work reliably with major streaming platforms.
  </p>

  <h3>Bypassing Internet Censorship</h3>
  <p>
    Countries like China, UAE, Russia, and Turkey restrict access to various websites and services. VPNs can bypass
    these blocks, though not all VPNs work in heavily restricted countries.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Important:</strong> Always research local laws regarding VPN use before traveling. While VPNs are legal in
    most countries, some restrict or ban their use.
  </p>

  <h3>Protecting Multiple Devices</h3>
  <p>
    As a digital nomad, you likely carry a laptop, phone, and possibly a tablet. Each device connecting to public WiFi
    is a potential vulnerability. VPN subscriptions typically cover multiple devices under one account.
  </p>

  <!-- Detailed Reviews -->
  <h2 id="detailed-reviews">VPN Detailed Reviews</h2>

  <!-- NordVPN -->
  <h3 id="nordvpn">1. NordVPN — Best Overall for Digital Nomads</h3>
  <p>
    NordVPN consistently ranks as our top recommendation for remote workers and digital nomads. It offers an excellent
    combination of strong security, fast speeds, and user-friendly apps across all platforms.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes NordVPN stand out:</strong> Their proprietary NordLynx protocol (based on WireGuard) delivers
    exceptional speeds while maintaining strong encryption. The Threat Protection feature blocks malware and trackers
    even when the VPN is disconnected—a nice security bonus.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>6,000+ servers in 111 countries:</strong> Excellent global coverage for digital nomads</li>
    <li><strong>NordLynx protocol:</strong> Blazing fast speeds with minimal impact on connection</li>
    <li><strong>Threat Protection:</strong> Blocks malware, trackers, and ads</li>
    <li><strong>Double VPN:</strong> Route traffic through two servers for extra security</li>
    <li><strong>Obfuscated servers:</strong> Works in China, UAE, and other restricted countries</li>
    <li><strong>No-logs policy:</strong> Independently audited by PwC and Deloitte</li>
    <li><strong>10 simultaneous devices:</strong> Cover all your devices and share with travel companions</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $3.39/month (2-year plan), $4.99/month (1-year plan), $12.99/month (monthly). All plans
    include a 30-day money-back guarantee.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Speed test results:</strong> In our testing, NordVPN reduced speeds by only 11% on average—barely noticeable
    for most activities. Video calls, large file uploads, and streaming all worked flawlessly.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Best for:</strong> Digital nomads who want the best balance of security, speed, and features. Especially
    good for those traveling to restricted countries or who need reliable streaming access.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Minor drawbacks:</strong> The 2-year commitment required for the best pricing may not suit short-term
    nomads. The desktop app can feel cluttered with its many features.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/nordvpn"
